Device configuration for the LGE LU5400 (LG Prada 3.0)

Build target
------------

    source build/envsetup.sh
    lunch cm_lu5400-userdebug

Source trees: device/lge/lu5400, kernel/lge/lu5400, vendor/lge/lu5400.
Kernel configuration: cyanogenmod_lu5400_defconfig.
Build output: out/target/product/lu5400.

The kernel still supports other P2 variants. P940-specific board selections
and the stock p2_p940_defconfig describe the separate international model;
the LU5400 build selects CONFIG_MACH_LGE_P2_LU5400.

Proprietary blobs
-----------------

proprietary-files.txt is the canonical blob manifest. Each entry uses:

    system/relative/path|sha1

Extract the known-good blobs from a connected, booted device:

    device/lge/lu5400/extract-files.sh

Alternatively, extract them from an unpacked system directory:

    device/lge/lu5400/extract-files.sh /path/to/system

All 55 files are staged and checked before vendor/lge/lu5400/proprietary is
replaced. A missing file or SHA-1 mismatch aborts extraction and preserves the
existing vendor tree. setup-makefiles.sh regenerates the vendor makefiles from
the same manifest without copying or storing the proprietary files in git.

Device-local graphics and camera compatibility
----------------------------------------------

hwc/ contains the CM11 LG OMAP4 HWC, its private headers, and the EDID parser.
It does not read sources from device/lge/p920.

The original camera.omap4.so expects legacy jhead functions through a
libexif.so dependency. camera/Android.mk builds the bundled camera/jhead sources
as a separate libjex.so, without changing or depending on external/libexif or
external/jhead. The short library name fits in the original ELF string slot.

camera/fixup_camera.py verifies the camera blob against proprietary-files.txt
and changes only that DT_NEEDED name in an intermediate copy. camera.lu5400
installs the result as system/lib/hw/camera.lu5400.so and requires libjex.
Android's HAL loader selects this file using ro.hardware=lu5400 before falling
back to the platform's camera.omap4.so. The vendor makefile
omits the raw camera copy to avoid overwriting the fixed module. The original
vendor blob and its extraction hash stay unchanged; extracting from a built
ROM's fixed camera will intentionally fail the original-blob hash check.

For later Android versions, retain this device-owned jhead implementation
instead of using the ROM's EXIF implementation. Android 7.1.2 in the local
android7 tree no longer includes external/jhead. Its Lineage linker supports
LINKER_FORCED_SHIM_LIBS as another way to inject a compatibility library, but
the CM11 implementation uses a direct ELF dependency and needs no linker patch.
This isolates EXIF compatibility only: camera HAL, libui/libgui, OMX, gralloc,
SELinux, and linker namespace changes still require validation for each port.
The original camera also has DT_TEXTREL. The supplied Android 7 linker supports
TARGET_NEEDS_PLATFORM_TEXT_RELOCATIONS in BoardConfig.mk for such platform
blobs; a later port must explicitly evaluate this requirement. No Android 7
device tree or framework source is modified by this CM11 change.
